The container image in this repository downloads and builds FET from the
official upstream source release (see the Dockerfile `FET_VERSION` /
`FET_URL` build args). FET's source is therefore obtainable from the same URL
the image is built from:

  https://lalescu.ro/liviu/fet/download.html

AGPL-3.0 network clause (section 13): because this service offers FET's
functionality to users over a network, operators must make the complete
corresponding source of the AGPL-covered program available to those users.
This repository builds the unmodified upstream binary; if you modify FET
itself, you must publish your modified FET source to your users as well.

This wrapper (the `app/` Python package, Dockerfile, and tests) is a separate
program that communicates with `fet-cl` only as a subprocess. It is likewise
distributed under AGPL-3.0-or-later to keep the combined service compliant.

This is a summary, not legal advice.
